node_modules
dist/
.astro/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
*.log
.claude/worktrees/

# Probe screenshots regenerate on every evidence run — the JSON logs are the evidence.
docs/verification/evidence/**/*.png

# Carve-out, and the rule for when it applies: keep the screenshots when there was no inspector to
# produce a log, so the image IS the only artifact. iOS WebKit has no inspector on this path, so
# gh#50's fifth box rests on frames a human reads — an ignored .png would make a closed ticket cite
# files that do not exist. A CDP probe never qualifies: it can always emit JSON.
!docs/verification/evidence/50/webkit/*.png
# gh#241: the owner picks a card-art style by looking at this sheet. Its content is a look, which no
# log can carry, so the image is the artifact the pick will cite (rebuild: make_compare.py beside it).
!docs/verification/evidence/gh241/compare-abc.png
# gh#242: same reason — the owner judges "the set reads as one style next to the pilot" off these sheets.
!docs/verification/evidence/gh242/set-*.png

# Design canvas build output — a ~2MB seeded bundle whose minified editor code
# trips added-lineno-citation-check. The .dc.html sources + canvas.json beside it are the real artifact.
# Matched by pattern, not by name: this entry named one filename until 2026-08-25, and renaming the
# bundle silently un-ignored 2.2MB with nothing complaining.
design/*.html
!design/*.dc.html
